  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;be any two events with positive probabilities&nbsp;<br /><br /><strong>Statement I:</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br /><strong>Statement II:</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both the statements are false",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both the statements are true",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement - <strong>I</strong> is false, Statement - <strong>II</strong> is true",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement - <strong>I</strong> is true, Statement - <strong>II</strong> is false",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>From the equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Again, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Both the statements are true.</p>"
  }
